{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "flowName": "gui-hero-cyd-onboard",
  "notes": "CYD GUI demo with no extra hardware and no WiFi. Three pages, changing every 8 s:\n- Light: the on-board LDR (GPIO 34) as 0-100 %, with a bar and a 6.4-minute trend (journal: 77 rows of 5 s).\n- Board: free memory and uptime.\n- Nearby: Bluetooth devices heard in the last 30 s, and the strongest three by signal.\n\nSetup:\n- Needs the roster custom node (mike/roster) in ~/.thingstudio/custom-nodes/.\n- Light is calibrated in the 'light' function (DARK_PERCENT, BRIGHT_PERCENT), from Mike's CYD. Another unit may need\n  its own: read the adc percent with the LDR covered and in dim light.\n- Hard-reset the board before deploying: Bluetooth needs an unfragmented heap.\n\nWhy no WiFi: with the GUI running, a classic ESP32 without PSRAM has ESP-IDF heap for one radio, not WiFi and\nBluetooth together. With a wifi status node in the flow, Deploy failed: \"Bluetooth radio failed to start\n(OSError(116,))\" (2026-11-18). If the board joins WiFi at boot for the editor link, turn that off too.\nWhy no chip temperature: the classic ESP32's sensor returns a fixed value.\n\nOpen items:\n- roster exists only in Mike's custom-nodes folder, so anyone else opening this flow gets a missing node. Ship it as\n  a seeded example node to make the demo work for testers.\n- The user docs don't mention the one-radio limit. Add a line to custom-firmware.md's \"Memory and the board\" or the\n  ble node page, so a tester doesn't hit the same deploy failure.",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "n01-ldr",
      "type": "thingstudio/adc",
      "properties": {
        "pin": 34,
        "mode": "relative",
        "delta": 500,
        "lower": 0,
        "upper": 50000,
        "sense": "outside",
        "pollMs": 2000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n02-light",
      "type": "thingstudio/function",
      "properties": {
        "code": "# The CYD's LDR (GPIO 34) as a light level, 0-100 %.\n# The adc node's payload is a dict: {'raw': counts, 'volts': ..., 'percent': raw as 0-100}.\n# Calibrate with the adc 'percent' at the two ends (Mike's CYD, 2026-11-18): covered by a hand, and in front of a\n# monitor in a dark room. On this board the LDR bottoms out there, so anything brighter also reads 100.\n# Either order works: a board whose reading rises with light just has BRIGHT_PERCENT above DARK_PERCENT.\nDARK_PERCENT = 75\nBRIGHT_PERCENT = 0\nlevel = (msg['payload']['percent'] - DARK_PERCENT) * 100 / (BRIGHT_PERCENT - DARK_PERCENT)\nmsg['payload'] = round(min(100, max(0, level)))\nreturn msg\n",
        "outputCount": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n03-lightval",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_readout",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Light",
        "units": "%",
        "decimals": 0,
        "lo": 0,
        "hi": 100,
        "staleAfter": 15
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n04-lightbar",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_bar",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Light bar",
        "lo": 0,
        "hi": 100,
        "staleAfter": 15
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n05-lighttrend",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_trend",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Light trend",
        "lo": 0,
        "hi": 100,
        "columns": 60,
        "colWidth": 3,
        "height": 60,
        "staleAfter": 30
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n06-tick",
      "type": "thingstudio/timer",
      "properties": {
        "intervalMs": 2000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n07-board",
      "type": "thingstudio/function",
      "properties": {
        "code": "# Board health, read every tick: free memory (kB) and minutes since the flow started.\n# time.time() counts seconds on the board's clock without wrapping, set or not, so the difference is the uptime.\nimport gc\nimport time\nstart = context.get('start', None)\nif start is None:\n    start = time.time()\n    context.set('start', start)\nmemory = {'topic': 'memory', 'payload': gc.mem_free() // 1024}\nuptime = {'topic': 'uptime', 'payload': (time.time() - start) // 60}\nreturn [memory, uptime]\n",
        "outputCount": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n09-mem",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_readout",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Free memory",
        "units": "kB",
        "decimals": 0,
        "lo": 0,
        "hi": 160,
        "staleAfter": 15
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n12-pagetick",
      "type": "thingstudio/timer",
      "properties": {
        "intervalMs": 8000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n13-next",
      "type": "thingstudio/function",
      "properties": {
        "code": "msg['payload'] = 'next'\nreturn msg\n",
        "outputCount": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n14-nav",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_navigator",
      "properties": {
        "name": "nav",
        "screen": ""
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n15-screen",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_screen",
      "properties": {
        "name": "tft",
        "minInterval": 200,
        "wrap": true,
        "gridColumns": 12,
        "gridRows": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n16-display",
      "type": "thingstudio/display_spi",
      "properties": {
        "controller": "st7789",
        "frameFormat": "gs4",
        "spiBus": 2,
        "baudrate": 27000000,
        "sck": 14,
        "mosi": 13,
        "dc": 2,
        "cs": 15,
        "reset": -1,
        "backlight": 21,
        "width": 240,
        "height": 320,
        "rotation": 1,
        "xstart": 0,
        "ystart": 0,
        "colorOrder": "bgr",
        "invertColors": false,
        "dataLatchOrder": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n17-lightjournal",
      "type": "thingstudio/journal",
      "properties": {
        "rows": 77,
        "stepSeconds": 5,
        "steps": 0,
        "xff": 0.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n18-ble",
      "type": "thingstudio/ble_scan",
      "properties": {
        "namePrefix": "",
        "addr": "",
        "mfrId": "",
        "serviceUuid": "",
        "active": true,
        "repeatMs": 1000,
        "scanIntervalMs": 320,
        "scanWindowMs": 100
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n22-blecount",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_readout",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Devices",
        "units": "",
        "decimals": 0,
        "lo": 0,
        "hi": 60,
        "staleAfter": 15
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n23-dev1",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_label",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Strongest 1",
        "maxChars": 15,
        "staleAfter": 15
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n24-dev2",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_label",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Strongest 2",
        "maxChars": 15,
        "staleAfter": 15
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n25-dev3",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_label",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Strongest 3",
        "maxChars": 15,
        "staleAfter": 15
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n19-roster",
      "type": "mike/roster",
      "properties": {
        "key": "addr",
        "timeoutS": 30,
        "expired": "drop",
        "merge": true,
        "maxEntries": 50,
        "sortBy": "rssi",
        "minIntervalMs": 2000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n21-format",
      "type": "thingstudio/function",
      "properties": {
        "code": "# The roster's list, sorted by signal, as the page's count and three label lines.\nitems = msg['payload']\nout = [{'topic': 'count', 'payload': msg['count']}]\nfor i in range(3):\n    if i < len(items):\n        item = items[i]\n        label = (item.get('name') or item['addr'][-8:])[:11]\n        out.append({'topic': 'device', 'payload': '%s %d' % (label, item['rssi'])})\n    else:\n        out.append({'topic': 'device', 'payload': ''})\nreturn out\n",
        "outputCount": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n26-uptime",
      "type": "thingstudio/gui_readout",
      "properties": {
        "name": "Uptime",
        "units": "min",
        "decimals": 0,
        "lo": 0,
        "hi": 1440,
        "staleAfter": 15
      }
    }
  ],
